    "narrative": "With the Austin Waves fighting to gain ground in the 5x5 standings, today\u2019s optimal lineup leans heavily into specific matchup advantages against weaker pitching rotations. **Miguel Vargas** leads our daily efficiency board with a 63.53 score; despite a neutral park environment, his favorable matchup against Abbott and a prime #3 spot in the order make him our most reliable anchor. **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** remains an elite play at 60.95, as his high recency rating offsets a tough test against Tolle. Meanwhile, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** offers the most intriguing upside of the day at 58.88; his strong platoon advantage against Gilbert, combined with the favorable park factors, positions him as a high-floor utility start that could easily outperform his projection.\n\nThe decision-making process was tightest at the bottom of the outfield, where **Wade Meckler** (42.25) and **Luis Lara** (44.52) narrowly edged out internal depth. While **Wade Meckler** benefits from a lead-off role, he faces a daunting matchup against the elite arm of deGrom, whose 3.13 xERA significantly suppresses our output ceiling. **Luis Lara** earns the nod based on his switch-hitting versatility against Sasaki, though both players are strictly \"marginal\" starts. We continue to monitor the status of **Jordan Westburg**, who remains sidelined on the IL, while our core contributors like **Gunnar Henderson**, **Luis Robert Jr.**, and **Jackson Merrill** are unfortunately off today due to scheduling. With the scarcity of stolen bases remaining a critical bottleneck, we are prioritizing these high-contact profiles to maintain efficiency while protecting our remaining game caps for the stretch run.",
